# BUG REPRO: #8944 over-drop on dns — head-gap check with a later BARE < rule.
#
# The dns query tx is first presented to detection at detect progress 0 (the tx is
# created in the started state and completes within the same packet: tx_progress 1,
# detect_progress_orig 0). The head candidate (accept:flow request_complete, hook 1)
# has a head-of-list gap (1 > detect_progress_orig 0) on the first detection pass,
# before the < rule has ever been inspected.
#
# The later accept:flow dns:<request_complete rule legitimately covers the gap
# (bare rule, no keyword — it auto-accepts the prior state and matches at
# completion). Correct behaviour: the query is accepted (no default app policy
# drop).
#
# main: no coverage suppression -> "missing fw rules at list start: sid 852,
#   progress 1 (1:0)" -> default app policy drop (over-drop, #8944 family).
# bug-8944-new/v3: max_in_progress_lte_hook is computed from stored rule state; the
#   < rule has never been inspected on the first pass, so it has no stored state and
#   does not count -> same over-drop.
# the #8944 fix (firewall-bug-8944-new/v5): max_in_progress_lte_hook is computed from
#   the final candidate list (this-pass prefilter candidates count) -> suppresses the
#   gap -> accept (correct here).
#
# Note: dns only has two progress states per direction (0 request_started, 1
# request_complete; the parser is transactional/stateless — every tx is complete at
# progress 1), so the shapes of the false-accept family (214/215/218 mirrors, d03/
# d04/d05 probes) do NOT reproduce here: a single-packet tx takes the tx-end
# stateful re-apply path, which all branches handle fail-closed.

# allow session setup
accept:hook udp:all 10.16.1.11 any <> 10.16.1.1 any (flow:not_established; sid:1021;)
accept:hook udp:all 10.16.1.11 any <> 10.16.1.1 any (flow:established; sid:1022;)
# bare head accept:flow at request_complete, followed by a later bare < rule
accept:flow dns:request_complete 10.16.1.11 any -> 10.16.1.1 any (sid:852;)
accept:flow dns:<request_complete 10.16.1.11 any -> 10.16.1.1 any (sid:853;)
